  <data name="Chat_Greet1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>👋 Hi! I am RoomFinder's automatic assistant. I can advise you on room area, amenities, the deposit-and-hold process, or how to use the map to find a room.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Greet2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>✨ Nice to meet you! Want me to show you how to filter rooms with a balcony or a private bathroom, or clear up anything about the deposit?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Greet3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🤖 Hello! I am the automatic support chatbot. Do you have any question about rent price, how long a room is held for you, or the VIP listing policy?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Slang1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🤖 Hey, take it easy! I am only an automatic assistant. Just type a keyword such as 'rent', 'amenities' or 'deposit' and I will give you the exact information.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Slang2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>💡 Confused? Ask a bit more clearly about a site feature or the room details (area, private bathroom...) so I can answer you properly.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Map" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🗺️ The system embeds a smart Leaflet map! Open 'Find room', pick your School and a search radius (km). The map measures the straight-line distance from each room's coordinates (latitude/longitude) right to the school gate.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Deposit" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>💰 Renters can pay the deposit straight through VNPay to hold a room. The holding period (number of days) is set by the landlord. If the deposit deadline passes without a signed contract, the system automatically releases the room for someone else so it stays fair.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Price1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>💵 Every listing on RoomFinder states the rent (VND/month) up front. On the room detail page you can see the exact size (length x width) and know in advance whether it has a balcony or a private bathroom.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Price2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>📏 The system requires landlords to declare the price, length and width of the room. You can also see at a glance on the detail screen whether the room has a private bathroom or a balcony.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Fraud" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🚩 To stop spam posts, every listing has an 'expiry date'. Rooms marked 'Already rented' are hidden from the list automatically. If a landlord fakes the area or scams your deposit, remember to press Report so an Admin can handle it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Vip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>⭐ Listings ticked as 'VIP' are pinned and shown first on both the list and the map. It is a handy way for landlords to find a renter faster.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Author" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🏫 RoomFinder was researched and built with ASP.NET Core MVC to give students a safe way to find a place to live.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_OffTopic" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🤖 I am the automatic assistant of the RoomFinder system, so I am only programmed to answer questions about the room-rental system.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Fallback1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>💡 I did not quite get that. Could you ask more clearly about the rent, the area (length, width), the amenities (balcony, bathroom) or how long a deposit holds the room?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Fallback2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>📬 That question is outside my data! You can message the landlord directly on the room detail page to get more information.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Chat_Fallback3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>🤖 If you are looking for a room, try filtering Province, District and School name on the search bar. The system computes the coordinates and reports the exact distance for you.</value>
  </data>
